      "end_line": 283,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/ReviewView.tsx",
      "content": "Overlay navigation also changes `trade` and `panel`, so stripping only these two parameters still treats opening/closing Replay as a fresh card link. For example, load `/review?trade=t1\u0026panel=Action`, manually open t2, then open and close its Replay. Back restores `trade=t1`, this effect selects t1 (and reads it again), and t2 closes instead of remaining on its Action panel. Distinguish overlay-owned history changes from actual incoming card links, and add a test starting from a URL naming a different card.",
      "existing_code": "    link.delete('replay');\n    link.delete('session');",
      "start_line": 476,
      "end_line": 477,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/ReviewCard.tsx",
      "content": "The copied query retains `instrument`. If Review was entered through an instrument link, then the user switches to Action and clicks Replay, `linkedCard` gives that retained instrument precedence over `panel=Action`. The resulting URL change reopens Marks under the overlay; after Close the Replay button is hidden and cannot receive focus. Remove the instrument selector from the overlay URL and ensure restoring the previous URL on Close does not reapply the old instrument link. Cover this instrument-link entry path in the tests.",
      "existing_code": "      next.set('trade', trade.tradeId);\n      next.set('panel', 'Action');\n      next.set('replay', 'open');",
